WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our first guest is
a very talented actress

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:05.234
who stars in the new movie
"The Lost Daughter,"

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.901
which is in select theaters
Friday

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.367
and streaming on Netflix
December 31st.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:12.634
Please welcome Dakota Johnson!

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:15.467
Ah! Yes, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.801
Ah!

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.267
I miss you.
It's always great to see you.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.801
-I miss you too.
And this is so sad.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.534
I mean, it's great.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.667
-Yeah. Thank you, yeah.
It's sad.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.167
Yeah, I wish you were here.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.834
But, yeah, you're doing well?

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.434
-I'm good. Yeah.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:34.567
-Good.
-I'm good.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.234
How are you doing?

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.601
-I'm doing good.

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.501
[ Laughter ]
-I'm so much bigger than you.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.434
I can see what I look like
next to you.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:44.100
-No, I like this size of you.
-And it's so weird.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.501
-We always want more of you,

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.834
so now we just made you actually
physically bigger now.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.367
Yeah, we love it.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.167
More Dakota Johnson the better,
that's what I say.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:56.968
Have to talk about this 'cause
the last time you were

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.133
on the show,
you were very funny.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:01.434
We were talking about
this article you did for

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:04.033
or a photo shoot spread you did
for "Architectural Digest"

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.467
or something of your home.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.334
And there was a bowl of limes
in the kitchen.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.901
Some people know
what I'm talking about.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:14.000
In the article you said like,
"Oh, yeah, I love limes"

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.467
or something like that.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.567
And then you came on our show.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.968
You said actually
you don't love them.

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.234
You said you're allergic
to limes.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.634
And it caused
a giant controversy.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:25.834
I mean, this is the --

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.133
This could have been
the end of your career.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:29.133
There was -- People wrote
articles. Look at this.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.767
"Dakota Johnson lied to us
about loving limes."

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:33.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:35.400
And this is major headlines.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.801
This is --

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.901
"Dakota Johnson
selling her house

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:40.567
and confessing she hates limes

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.000
is the biggest plot twist
of 2021."

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.501
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:47.300
Feels like there was way more
important news than that.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.734
-Are you aware of the fallout?

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.601
I mean, how are you dealing with
this crisis?

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.834
-Well, it's been really hard,
Jimmy.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.734
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:58.701
Do you not like limes?

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:02.067
-I don't really care
about limes.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:06.934
I love them and I also found out
after I did "Arch Digest."

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.968
I did that, and, you know,
they have somebody

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.133
who is super talented

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:14.200
come in and make your house
look amazing.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.400
So they put this
big bowl of limes,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.734
which I saw
while we were filming.

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.167
And it was funny.

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:23.767
So I talked about it because
who has a bowl of only limes?

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.601
Apparently me.
-Apparently you.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:29.634
-And then I did an allergy test
a few weeks later,

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:32.100
and it turns out
that I'm allergic to limes.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.100
But I never knew because usually

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.267
when I have them they're
in, like, a tequila.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.334
[ Laughter ]
So...

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.701
-Yeah. That's kind of -- Yeah.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.834
Is there anything else you're
allergic to so we can get it out

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:44.267
of the way now so there's
no more controversy?

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.701
-Yes.
Thank you so much for asking.

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:50.267
I'm so excited to have this
be in the news too.

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:52.367
I'm allergic to soy.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:53.868
-There you go.
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.934
Wow. Yeah, there you go.
There you go, the reaction.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.601
-Don't send me any edamame
this Christmas season.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:01.167
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.033
Yeah, we're not going to get you
any edamame.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.300
What are you doing
for the holidays?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.200
Do you have any plans?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.200
-I'm going to be at home
with my family.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.868
Some of my family
is coming to my house.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:15.267
-Oh, that -- So you're hosting
the whole family?

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:18.801
Is that stressful?

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:20.801
-I haven't really thought
about it.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.467
[ Laughter ]
It's fast approaching, isn't it?

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.801
-Yeah, it's like next week,
yeah.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:26.167
You really have to -- Yeah.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.200
You have to plan something.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.367
-No, I don't.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.300
[ Laughter ]
-You have to get, like, food.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.000
You have to do something.
You have to entertain.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.467
What are you --
You gonna play games?

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.701
Do you play board games?
-Yeah. Well, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.634
Games for sure.
We'll do, like, Scrabble

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:40.567
and all the, you know,
the games.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:44.400
But, like, I feel like it's
better and more relaxing

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.100
for everybody if they just
fend for themselves.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.501
-Wait, what?

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.167
Wait, so your parents
come and you go,

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.367
"Yeah, look, if you're hungry,
you're an adult.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.167
Get something."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.434
-Exactly. They're all grown-ups.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:00.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:03.934
-What's your go-to
Scrabble word? Do you have one?

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:05.000
I have a great one for you.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.801
-Does anyone have a go-to
Scrabble word?

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:08.067
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:10.167
Oh, I definitely have mine.
-That's impossible.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.400
-No. I'll tell it to you
and it'll be yours.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.868
-What is it?

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.667
-"Za."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:18.300
-Oh, like short for pizza?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.634
-Yeah.
Pizza's too long of a word.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:20.801
-Some za?

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.868
-Pizza's too long of a word
for me to say.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:24.534
So I call it Za.
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:29.901
It's in the Scrabble dictionary.
"Za" is a real word.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:32.934
-It is, it is.
-Changes the whole game.

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:36.934
-Isn't -- So is J-A?

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.200
-J-O.
-Q-A.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.234
-Q-A?
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:42.901
-I'm going to challenge you
on that one.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.968
-I'm really good at Scrabble.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:47.167
-We'll play next time
you come on.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.834
Are you going to watch
any holiday movies?

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:53.934
-I really love --
Okay, my whole life --

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:55.767
Well, no, not my whole life.
That's intense.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:58.400
But when I was little, I went
through a phase where I watched

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.100
"Home Alone"
every day of the year.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.968
-Every single day you watched
"Home Alone"?

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.133
-Every day.
-Wow.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.901
-I was really into it.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.167
-I was like that with
"Pee-wee's Big Adventure."

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:13.667
[ Laughter ]
I watched it every single day.

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:14.868
Memorized every line.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:16.667
Used to do impersonations of
everybody.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.300
I loved it so much, I mean --
-Yeah.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.667
-If I quizzed you on
"Home Alone,"

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:22.300
do you think you'd do well?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.534
-I think maybe -- I don't know.
Maybe. Let's try.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.467
Do you have a question?
-I have some questions. I do.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:31.367
-Oh [bleep], okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.067
-Can you say that --
-Sorry.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.367
-Can you say that on TV?
No, you can't.

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:37.234
-Oh, shoot!
-Thank you.

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:38.634
-Is what I meant.

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.934
-Alright, ready for this?
-Yeah.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.534
-What are the burglars'
first names?

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:47.000
-Harry and Marv.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.234
-Wow! That is correct!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:50.701
Hey, I thought that was
a hard one.

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:53.968
-That's simple.
-That's an easy one for you?

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:55.801
-Okay. Come on.
-Alright.

00:05:55.801 --> 00:06:00.234
What do the burglars
refer to themselves as

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:02.400
in the first "Home Alone" movie?

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.133
What do they call themselves?

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:06.367
-"The Wet Bandits."

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:07.934
-Wow, that's completely correct.
-Because they --

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.434
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.334
-They leave the bathtubs
running.

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:14.801
They leave the water
running in the houses.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:17.534
-Wow, that's right.
-That's their calling card.

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:20.167
-Wow! This is -- This is
fantastic that you know so much.

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:21.734
Alright, how about --
This is a tough one.

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.934
What is the name of the movie
that Kevin watches

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:25.534
while eating ice cream?

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:30.601
-It's not a real movie.
It's, um...

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:31.734
It's a fake movie.

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:34.701
It's called...

00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:36.934
"Angels" something.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:39.567
Oh, sh--
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:41.200
-Yes.
-"Dirty Angels"?

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.334
"Dirty, Dirty Angels"?
-No.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.934
"Dirty, Dirty Angels,"
but very close.

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:48.367
"Angels with Filthy Souls."

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:49.968
-Oh, same thing.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:52.200
[ Ding! ]
-We gave you credit for that?

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:56.000
We gave you credit for it.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.167
The judges like you here.

00:06:58.167 --> 00:06:59.501
Okay, what character does

00:06:59.501 --> 00:07:01.934
Macaulay Culkin's brother
Kieran Culkin play?

00:07:06.701 --> 00:07:09.634
-Fuller because --
And he wets the bed.

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:10.934
[ Laughs ]
-Wow.

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.033
-Is that right?
-That is correct.

00:07:12.033 --> 00:07:13.400
[ Ding! ]
Fuller. That's right.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:17.667 --> 00:07:19.501
Okay.

00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:21.801
-Can I tell you something
quickly just like as a --

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:24.434
just, like, an intermission
from the game?

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.934
-Yeah.
-I saw Macaulay Culkin recently.

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:29.300
And I've never seen him
in real life,

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:34.000
but I saw him because he was
walking in the Gucci show.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.334
-Was he really?

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:38.501
-And I was sho-ck-ed.

00:07:38.501 --> 00:07:40.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:42.200
-You made that word
three syllables.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.634 --> 00:07:46.400
Sho-ck-ed?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:52.968
Wow. Because you're such a fan?

00:07:52.968 --> 00:07:56.434
-Well, logically, like, I know
that he's grown up, you know.

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:58.968
But then when you see him,
he's a man.

00:07:58.968 --> 00:08:00.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:01.968
And he was a man
wearing Gucci clothes,

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:03.968
just walking down
Hollywood Boulevard.

00:08:03.968 --> 00:08:06.267
-Yeah. He is a man, yeah.

00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:07.968
It's unbelievable.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.968 --> 00:08:10.701
Can we talk about
your new movie?

00:08:10.701 --> 00:08:12.534
-Oh, we're not going to finish
the game?

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:14.133
[ Laughter ]
'Cause I was going to win?

00:08:14.133 --> 00:08:15.300
-I feel like it's too easy.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.300
You're getting all of them
right.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.601
I mean, you're clearly a fan.

00:08:18.601 --> 00:08:21.133
I'll ask you one last one.
Ready?

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.167
What gift does the fake
Santa Claus give Kevin?

00:08:26.167 --> 00:08:27.834
-Oh, Tic Tacs.

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:29.067
-Wow!
[ Ding! ]

00:08:29.067 --> 00:08:30.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is unbelievable!

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:32.667
You're a fan!

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:36.100
You're amazing! You really are
a fan. I love that.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.234
Next time you come on,
you can ask me questions

00:08:38.234 --> 00:08:40.834
about "Pee-wee's Big Adventure."
-Okay.

00:08:40.834 --> 00:08:43.501
-I want to talk about your new
movie, "The Lost Daughter."

00:08:43.501 --> 00:08:44.901
Congrats, by the way.

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:47.334
Today it got two Golden Globe
nominations.

00:08:47.334 --> 00:08:49.234
So that's always good to get.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:51.667
Two Critics Choice Award noms.

00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:53.767
Nom, nom, nom, nom.

00:08:53.767 --> 00:08:54.968
This is --
-Nom, nom, nom.

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:56.534
-Yeah. Nom, nom, nom.

00:08:56.534 --> 00:08:58.334
Tell everyone what it's about.

00:08:58.334 --> 00:09:00.634
Can you explain the movie?

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:02.501
-"The Lost Daughter" is a movie

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:05.000
based on the book
by Elena Ferrante.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.767
And it is about a woman who is
vacationing on a beach.

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:12.834
And she becomes sort of obsessed

00:09:12.834 --> 00:09:15.434
with this young mother
and her daughter,

00:09:15.434 --> 00:09:18.400
who seem to be having
a troubling time.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.000
The young woman is
kind of struggling with

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.968
difficult things in her life.
-Yeah.

00:09:22.968 --> 00:09:26.734
-And I play that person.
Her name is Nina.

00:09:26.734 --> 00:09:30.133
And it's with Olivia Colman
and Jessie Buckley

00:09:30.133 --> 00:09:33.133
and loads of other
supremely talented people.

00:09:33.133 --> 00:09:34.934
And Maggie Gyllenhaal
directed it.

00:09:34.934 --> 00:09:37.734
And it is pretty intense.

00:09:37.734 --> 00:09:40.067
-Yeah. Congrats on being in
such an awesome film.

00:09:40.067 --> 00:09:42.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:09:42.167 --> 00:09:45.033
-Well deserved, buddy.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:45.033 --> 00:09:47.701
Here's Dakota Johnson
in "The Lost Daughter."

00:09:47.701 --> 00:09:48.968
Take a look at this.

00:09:48.968 --> 00:09:53.033
-So she's not calming down.
[ Child crying ]

00:09:53.033 --> 00:09:54.133
-Yeah.

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:56.467
-Mommy!

00:09:56.467 --> 00:09:59.133
-It's been a weird day.

00:09:59.133 --> 00:10:03.033
We found her and then she lost
her doll.

00:10:05.767 --> 00:10:07.501
-I used to have a doll
like that.

00:10:07.501 --> 00:10:08.801
Called Mina.

00:10:08.801 --> 00:10:10.767
-Nina?
-Mina.

00:10:10.767 --> 00:10:14.234
Or Mini Mama
as my mother called her.

00:10:14.234 --> 00:10:15.801
You'll find it.

00:10:15.801 --> 00:10:16.934
-Yeah.

00:10:16.934 --> 00:10:24.467
[ Crying continues ]

00:10:24.467 --> 00:10:26.100
-See you tomorrow.

00:10:28.767 --> 00:10:30.868
-Dakota Johnson, everybody!

00:10:30.868 --> 00:10:33.267
"The Lost Daughter" is
in select theaters Friday

00:10:33.267 --> 00:10:36.133
and streaming on Netflix
December 31st.

